course: dictionary
lesson: 6048
title: Menopause: a natural stage of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Menopause is a science word for a stage in a woman's life. It is the time, usually in middle age, when her monthly periods stop for good and she can no longer have babies. Read the clues around the word: "middle age", "stop for good" and "no longer have babies" all tell you what it means.
explain: «"The change" means the menopause, the time in middle age when a woman stops being able to have babies; it is old-fashioned.» Here the dictionary tells you that "the change" is an older, informal way of saying the same thing. When you meet a new word, check whether the text gives you a simpler word for it.
explain: Menopause is a natural stage of life, not an illness. Some women have hot flushes or feel tired during it, so health and science lessons teach about it as part of how the human body changes as people grow older.
fact: Menopause means the time when a woman's monthly periods stop for good.
fact: Menopause usually happens in middle age, and after it a woman can no longer have babies.
fact: Menopause is a natural stage of life, not an illness.
fact: Hot flushes and tiredness can happen during menopause.
fact: "The change" is an old-fashioned way of saying menopause.
exercise: What is menopause? | The time when a baby is born | *The time, usually in middle age, when a woman's monthly periods stop for good | The time when a child starts school
exercise: In the sentence «"The change" means the menopause...», which phrase is an old-fashioned way of saying menopause? | Middle age | *The change | A woman
exercise: Is menopause an illness? | *No, it is a natural stage of life | Yes, it is a serious disease that must be cured | Yes, it happens to every child at birth
test: During menopause, what happens to a woman's monthly periods? | They happen twice a month | *They stop for good | They start for the first time | They become very heavy every month
test: Jayden asks, "Is menopause a sickness?" What is the best answer? | Only if a woman is very young | Yes, it is a sickness that needs medicine every day | *No, it is a natural stage of life, though it can cause hot flushes | Yes, because it happens to babies
exam: Which fact about menopause is correct? | It is an illness that starts in childhood | It means a woman has just started her periods | It is the same thing as a baby being born | *It is a natural time, usually in middle age, when a woman's periods stop for good
